msgid "How-to Guides"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Task-oriented recipes, grouped by workspace. Each guide assumes basic "
"familiarity with EMStudio (see :ref:`tutorial`) and helps you reach one "
"objective."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`files/index`: open, save and reopen; a project folder; integrate "
"another file; find missing files; clean the file; pin a version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`bring-in/index`: files as documents, a geophysical stack, a GraphML"
" matrix, a table through a mapping, StratiMiner, a DosCo folder."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`stratigraphy/index`: units and their relations, groups, layout, "
"chronology, many units at once, filters."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`sources/index`: the provenance of files, documents and media on a "
"unit, regions traced on images, anomalies traced on geophysical slices."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`space/index`: georeferencing, models and tilesets, colours and "
"legend, placing objects, containers and epochs."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`sheets/index`: fill the recording sheet and print the sheets."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`archive/index`: files on disk and in the room, the shelf, versions "
"for each use, consolidation for a target."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`narrative/index`: write the story, show the graph in it, draft with"
" AI, export."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`rooms/index`: sign in, create a room, bring a file into a room, "
"enter and share it, open it in the other editor."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`extensions/index`: live work with EM Tools in Blender, a .blend "
"from the graph, vocabularies, packages and plugins, repositories and "
"signatures, the Python console."
msgstr ""

